  "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the time the full charge lasts. Then we have $X\u223cN(32,{4}^{2}).$\n\nWe want to find $P(X\\ge 36).$ Thus, we convert $X$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 36) & =P(Z\\ge \\frac{36-32}{4}) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge 1) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le 1) \\\\  & =1-\u03a6(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\n1-\u03a6(1)=1-0.8413\u22480.1587.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a full charge lasts $36$ hours or more is approximately $0.16.$",
